      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Subarachnoid hemorrhage (SAH) is common in clinical practice. SAH associated with vasculitis is rare. We present an unusually interesting case of SAH from a vertebral artery aneurysm in a young woman found to have advanced renal impairment."},
